WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.530 --> 00:00:04.660
Thanks in part to the San Diego Comic-Con,
July saw the release of some of the biggest

00:00:04.660 --> 00:00:06.720
movie trailers of the year so far.

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:10.669
From a tantalizing first look at Godzilla:
King of the Monsters to full-blown trailers

00:00:10.669 --> 00:00:15.829
for blockbusters like Overlord, Shazam, and
Fantastic Beasts 2, July came in like a lion

00:00:15.829 --> 00:00:20.510
and left like a kaiju, leaving a trail of
explosive movie mayhem in its wake.

00:00:20.510 --> 00:00:24.720
In fact, there are almost too many to keep
track of, so here's a rundown of all the best

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:29.380
trailers from July 2018 that are guaranteed
to get you excited.

00:00:29.380 --> 00:00:31.540
A Prayer Before Dawn

00:00:31.540 --> 00:00:34.980
So far, A24 is the studio that can't seem
to miss.

00:00:34.980 --> 00:00:39.510
They've been behind Oscar winners, underground
favorites, and blockbusters alike, and 2018

00:00:39.510 --> 00:00:43.100
sees them continuing that trend with A Prayer
Before Dawn.

00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:47.079
Following a British boxer who's sentenced
to stay in a violent Thailand prison, the

00:00:47.079 --> 00:00:51.460
film looks like a gritty character study and
a thrilling drama that won't pull any punches.

00:00:51.460 --> 00:00:55.749
Early screenings have already garnered A Prayer
Before Dawn an impressive Rotten Tomatoes

00:00:55.749 --> 00:00:59.350
score, and mainstream audiences will get the
chance to witness the inspiring story when

00:00:59.350 --> 00:01:02.309
it hits theaters on August 10th.

00:01:02.309 --> 00:01:03.809
Patient Zero

00:01:03.809 --> 00:01:08.060
After a relatively infection-free couple years,
zombies are breaking out on the big screen

00:01:08.060 --> 00:01:09.840
again with Patient Zero.

00:01:09.840 --> 00:01:13.650
Matt Smith plays an American soldier who can
communicate with the infected.

00:01:13.650 --> 00:01:17.210
His job is to sit down and chat with the zombies
in an attempt to figure out how the whole

00:01:17.210 --> 00:01:18.210
plague works.

00:01:18.210 --> 00:01:22.910
But he meets his match when one zombie seems
to be different from all the rest.

00:01:22.910 --> 00:01:27.750
It turns out that the zombies probably aren't
zombies after all, they're more like smarter

00:01:27.750 --> 00:01:29.234
humans who happen to be really violent.

00:01:29.234 --> 00:01:30.640
"I don't think that we're the disease.

00:01:30.640 --> 00:01:34.200
We're the cure."

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:37.630
Can humanity survive against a better version
of themselves?

00:01:37.630 --> 00:01:42.630
Find out when Patient Zero goes straight to
streaming on August 14th.

00:01:42.630 --> 00:01:44.090
Assassination Nation

00:01:44.090 --> 00:01:49.060
Seeming to revel in its own controversy, Assassination
Nation released its second trailer in July

00:01:49.060 --> 00:01:53.840
and provided more glimpses into what's shaping
up to be a really weird movie world.

00:01:53.840 --> 00:01:58.450
The film centers on the breakdown of civilized
society in a small town after a hacker releases

00:01:58.450 --> 00:02:01.770
a bunch of emails and texts sent around by
the residents.

00:02:01.770 --> 00:02:06.049
It's all out war in the sleepy suburbs after
that, and the trailer descends into a montage

00:02:06.049 --> 00:02:08.959
of Purge-like violence between neighbors and
friends.

00:02:08.959 --> 00:02:11.739
Take a look on September 21st.

00:02:11.739 --> 00:02:13.370
Bohemian Rhapsody

00:02:13.370 --> 00:02:18.250
Each new trailer for Bohemian Rhapsody reveals
more details about the story, more glimpses

00:02:18.250 --> 00:02:22.349
of Rami Malek as Freddie Mercury, and, best
of all, more Queen songs.

00:02:22.349 --> 00:02:26.890
The hard-rocking biopic follows the band from
its humble origins to the sold-out stadiums,

00:02:26.890 --> 00:02:29.530
with a hard focus on frontman Freddie Mercury.

00:02:29.530 --> 00:02:32.660
"Roger there's only room in this band for
one hysterical queen."

00:02:32.660 --> 00:02:36.569
But of course, there's a dark side to every
story, and the latest trailer for Bohemian

00:02:36.569 --> 00:02:40.459
Rhapsody spares a few seconds to show that
it's not all foot-stomping, crowd-pleasing

00:02:40.459 --> 00:02:42.010
fun for this rock quartet.

00:02:42.010 --> 00:02:45.530
Bohemian Rhapsody doesn't look like it's going
to shy away from anything.

00:02:45.530 --> 00:02:49.040
Find out when it premieres on November 2nd.

00:02:49.040 --> 00:02:50.040
Overlord

00:02:50.040 --> 00:02:53.010
Despite all the rumors and speculation, producer
J.J.

00:02:53.010 --> 00:02:56.740
Abrams has always said that Overlord isn't
a Cloverfield movie.

00:02:56.740 --> 00:02:59.330
Nobody believes him, but that's what he's
saying, at least.

00:02:59.330 --> 00:03:03.599
So maybe we can all just enjoy it for what
it is, which is a World War II zombie movie.

00:03:03.599 --> 00:03:04.810
Is that so bad, really?

00:03:04.810 --> 00:03:09.300
The trailer opens with a plane full of soldiers
flying over the beaches of Normandy.

00:03:09.300 --> 00:03:13.299
Almost immediately, they're shot down, sending
a few of the unlucky troopers parachuting

00:03:13.299 --> 00:03:15.319
deep behind enemy lines.

00:03:15.319 --> 00:03:19.510
That would be bad enough, because Nazis, but
it turns out that there have been some devious

00:03:19.510 --> 00:03:23.980
Nazi experiments going on behind closed doors,
putting the intrepid band of soldiers face

00:03:23.980 --> 00:03:26.020
to face with horrifying monsters.

00:03:26.020 --> 00:03:30.060
It looks like a bucket of fun, and you can
check it out when Overlord hits theaters on

00:03:30.060 --> 00:03:32.420
November 9th.

00:03:32.420 --> 00:03:33.939
Boy Erased

00:03:33.939 --> 00:03:37.990
Joel Edgerton made his first foray into writing,
directing, and acting all in the same movie

00:03:37.990 --> 00:03:43.010
with 2015's The Gift, and his upcoming film
Boy Erased will see him back in all those

00:03:43.010 --> 00:03:44.010
roles.

00:03:44.010 --> 00:03:47.650
This time, he'll be tackling the story of
a young man forced into gay conversion therapy

00:03:47.650 --> 00:03:50.020
by his overbearing Baptist father.

00:03:50.020 --> 00:03:54.010
While Edgerton has a supporting role, the
main cast is anchored by Nicole Kidman and

00:03:54.010 --> 00:03:58.209
Russell Crowe, who star as the parents of
Jared, played by Lucas Hedges.

00:03:58.209 --> 00:04:02.530
The trailer is an emotional gut-punch from
start to finish, with gripping performances

00:04:02.530 --> 00:04:03.950
by everyone involved.

00:04:03.950 --> 00:04:08.549
And the fact that it's all based on a true
story twists the knife just a little bit deeper.

00:04:08.549 --> 00:04:11.990
Take a look when it lands in theaters on November
2nd.

00:04:11.990 --> 00:04:14.299
Fantastic Beasts: The Crimes of Grindelwald

00:04:14.299 --> 00:04:16.470
At this point, the Wizarding World of J.K.

00:04:16.470 --> 00:04:20.049
Rowling couldn't be stopped even if you hit
it with an Unforgivable Curse.

00:04:20.049 --> 00:04:25.050
In a year filled with huge blockbusters, Fantastic
Beasts: The Crimes of Grindelwald is still

00:04:25.050 --> 00:04:27.820
one of the most hotly anticipated films of
2018.

00:04:27.820 --> 00:04:33.300
Newt Scamander is back in action, and this
time he's being drafted by a young Albus Dumbledore

00:04:33.300 --> 00:04:37.360
to help bring down the scourge of the wizarding
world, Gellert Grindelwald.

00:04:37.360 --> 00:04:41.610
The trailer promises another magical adventure
filled with high-stakes wizardry and flying

00:04:41.610 --> 00:04:45.620
carriage chases, and, of course, plenty of
fantastic beasts.

00:04:45.620 --> 00:04:49.660
David Yates, who directed the first Fantastic
Beasts and the last four Harry Potter movies,

00:04:49.660 --> 00:04:51.940
returns to helm the Crimes of Grindelwald.

00:04:51.940 --> 00:04:55.020
Look for it on November 16th.

00:04:55.020 --> 00:04:56.020
Robin Hood

00:04:56.020 --> 00:04:59.940
Assassin's Creed heads to Nottingham in the
newest trailer for Robin Hood, the latest

00:04:59.940 --> 00:05:03.500
take on the legend that's putting the aerial
acrobatics back in archery.

00:05:03.500 --> 00:05:08.000
Kingsman's Taron Egerton stars as the hooded
arrow-slinger, with Jamie Foxx stepping in

00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:10.090
as his right-hand man Little John.

00:05:10.090 --> 00:05:13.721
Obviously, this rendition is taking a few
liberties with the source material, Little

00:05:13.721 --> 00:05:18.460
John is Robin's combat trainer, Maid Marian
is Irish instead of English, and none of them

00:05:18.460 --> 00:05:19.639
seem to be wearing tights.

00:05:19.639 --> 00:05:21.860
"You gotta be a man to wear tights."

00:05:21.860 --> 00:05:26.400
But we're assuming it'll make up for all that
with tons of action and epic bow-and-arrowing,

00:05:26.400 --> 00:05:29.580
mixed in with just enough romance to keep
everyone's dates happy.

00:05:29.580 --> 00:05:33.850
Robin Hood is scheduled to hit theaters on
November 21st.

00:05:33.850 --> 00:05:34.850
Aquaman

00:05:34.850 --> 00:05:38.120
Could this be the movie that defines the new
Worlds of DC?

00:05:38.120 --> 00:05:41.991
We're ready for one of these movies to come
out and blow us all away, and so far, all

00:05:41.991 --> 00:05:45.130
signs point to Aquaman being the one to do
it.

00:05:45.130 --> 00:05:49.280
Experienced filmmaker James Wan is in the
directing chair, and Jason Momoa seems to

00:05:49.280 --> 00:05:52.520
have all the right aqua-stuff to play the
king of Atlantis.

00:05:52.520 --> 00:05:57.061
The trailer shows that the film will be pulling
from Geoff Johns' 2011 Aquaman comics, which

00:05:57.061 --> 00:06:01.020
feature cool deep-sea critters called The
Trench and include a battle for the throne

00:06:01.020 --> 00:06:03.800
against Aquaman's own half brother, Orm.

00:06:03.800 --> 00:06:07.840
That's all good stuff, and the Aquaman trailer
seems to showcase plenty of style.

00:06:07.840 --> 00:06:11.479
Right now, Aquaman is slated to hit theaters
on December 21st.

00:06:11.479 --> 00:06:13.610
Alita: Battle Angel

00:06:13.610 --> 00:06:17.789
December 21st is shaping up to be a battleground
for box office dominance.

00:06:17.789 --> 00:06:21.550
Not only are Robin Hood and Aquaman hitting
the big screen that day, but they'll do so

00:06:21.550 --> 00:06:24.080
right alongside Alita: Battle Angel.

00:06:24.080 --> 00:06:28.419
With Robert Rodriguez directing from a script
co-written by James Cameron, this adaptation

00:06:28.419 --> 00:06:32.680
of the popular manga is in great hands, but
that hasn't stopped fans of the source material

00:06:32.680 --> 00:06:34.229
from getting kinda nervous.

00:06:34.229 --> 00:06:35.630
Why are they so squirrelly?

00:06:35.630 --> 00:06:38.270
Three words: Giant freaky eyes.

00:06:38.270 --> 00:06:42.860
True to the manga, the main character's eyes
are at least three sizes too large, or approximately

00:06:42.860 --> 00:06:46.160
the size of the Grinch's heart after he learns
the meaning of Christmas.

00:06:46.160 --> 00:06:49.979
Once you start looking past the obvious, though,
it's hard not to hope that Alita: Battle Angel

00:06:49.979 --> 00:06:52.330
could very tell turn out to be a great movie.

00:06:52.330 --> 00:06:56.240
The trailer shows off a beautifully stylized
future world, and if there's a good story

00:06:56.240 --> 00:07:01.009
behind it, then everyone may just end up forgetting
about those eyes after all.

00:07:01.009 --> 00:07:02.009
Glass

00:07:02.009 --> 00:07:06.810
Ever since the final scene of Split, audiences
have been waiting for the inevitable Splunbreakable

00:07:06.810 --> 00:07:08.400
crossover to materialize.

00:07:08.400 --> 00:07:12.590
Now that the first trailer for the sequel
is here, titled Glass after Samuel L. Jackson's

00:07:12.590 --> 00:07:16.210
Unbreakable character, it's starting to look
like the wait was worth it.

00:07:16.210 --> 00:07:18.180
The trailer doesn't hold back on the goods,
either.

00:07:18.180 --> 00:07:22.750
It jumps straight into a shot of Jackson's
Mr. Glass, Bruce Willis' David Dunn, and James

00:07:22.750 --> 00:07:25.680
McAvoy's Kevin Crumb sitting in a room together.

00:07:25.680 --> 00:07:28.990
After that, the trailer spends most of its
runtime making sure everyone knows who these

00:07:28.990 --> 00:07:30.000
people are.

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:34.669
Dunn is a bulletproof vigilante, Crumb is
a schizophrenic demon-man, and Glass is really

00:07:34.669 --> 00:07:36.120
really good at planning stuff.

00:07:36.120 --> 00:07:39.650
Finally, we get some hints that Glass and
Crumb are going to team up, and Dunn will

00:07:39.650 --> 00:07:41.629
have to stop their evil schemes.

00:07:41.629 --> 00:07:44.770
Check it out on January 18th, 2019.

00:07:44.770 --> 00:07:45.870
Shazam!

00:07:45.870 --> 00:07:51.819
Billy Batson may not be the most popular name
among the DC lineup, but even non-comics readers

00:07:51.819 --> 00:07:55.110
are bound to know the name of his alter ego:
Shazam.

00:07:55.110 --> 00:07:56.530
The first trailer for Shazam!

00:07:56.530 --> 00:07:59.479
introduces the young foster kid who's granted
superpowers.

00:07:59.479 --> 00:08:02.900
Like any kid, he just wants to have fun with
his new abilities, but when a supervillain

00:08:02.900 --> 00:08:07.220
menace starts making his presence known, Billy
will have to get serious to save the world.

00:08:07.220 --> 00:08:11.460
Zachary Levi seems like a great choice to
play the hero, especially since he seems to

00:08:11.460 --> 00:08:15.960
have such a great on-screen vibe with Dylan
Grazer, who's playing Billy's foster brother,

00:08:15.960 --> 00:08:16.960
Freddy Freeman.

00:08:16.960 --> 00:08:17.960
Shazam!

00:08:17.960 --> 00:08:20.009
strikes theaters sometime in April 2019.

00:08:20.009 --> 00:08:22.360
Godzilla: King of the Monsters

00:08:22.360 --> 00:08:26.629
July rewarded fans with two new looks at what's
to come for Godzilla: King of the Monsters.

00:08:26.629 --> 00:08:30.490
The month started with a brief teaser showing
Stranger Things' Millie Bobby Brown trying

00:08:30.490 --> 00:08:32.470
to get in touch with someone on a radio.

00:08:32.470 --> 00:08:36.530
But the big reveal came when the full-length
trailer for the movie dropped, because this

00:08:36.530 --> 00:08:39.670
time we actually got to see all those giant
monsters.

00:08:39.670 --> 00:08:43.530
Director Michael Dougherty has also teased
that a character from Kong: Skull Island will

00:08:43.530 --> 00:08:44.530
show up.

00:08:44.530 --> 00:08:47.280
"But we do bring back one character from Kong:
Skull Island."

00:08:47.280 --> 00:08:48.280
"Oh yeah?

00:08:48.280 --> 00:08:49.280
Which one is that?"

00:08:49.280 --> 00:08:50.540
"You'll have to see the movie."

00:08:50.540 --> 00:08:53.160
Hopefully that "character" is none other than
Kong himself.

00:08:53.160 --> 00:08:57.330
We'll be able to find out when Godzilla: King
of the Monsters smashes into theaters on May

00:08:57.330 --> 00:08:58.950
31, 2019.

